# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# WhatsApp session credentials (private keys — never commit, never deploy
# via the image; the production directory is bind-mounted instead)
/data/whatsapp-session/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Vitrine Inteligente — Henrique visual-reference preservation (owner's
# directive, 2026-11-21: "os arquivos de referência preservados não serão
# incluídos acidentalmente em commits"). The real reference PNG is
# intentionally NOT committed yet — committing it is a separate, explicit
# decision once the one-shot architecture itself is authorized for real
# use. Until then this stays structurally un-stageable by a broad `git
# add`, not just a habit to remember.
/docs/henrique-visual-reference/
# Real root cause fixed, 2026-11-21 (PR #17 review, "referência visual no
# deploy"): moved from lib/services/ai-creative-factory/assets/ (inside
# the app source tree, lost on every image rebuild) to this host-bind-
# mounted path (see docker-compose.prod.yml + docs/DEPLOYMENT.md) — still
# never committed, now also never silently lost on deploy.
/data/vitrine-creative-reference/
# Host-bind-mounted real generated creative files (docker-compose.prod.yml)
# — never committed, same reasoning as vitrine-creative-reference above.
# Noticed untracked during local (non-Docker) test runs on 2026-11-24.
/data/vitrine-creatives/

# Black Friday 2026 — raw import staging (extracted zips + the full
# hashed/deduplicated working set Henrique's files went through before
# scripts/seed-black-friday-2026.ts copied the real 34 into
# public/black-friday-2026/). Intermediate working data only, never the
# source of truth — safe to delete/recreate locally, never committed.
/.black-friday-2026-staging/
